# SQL Analytics and Data Warehouse Standards

## Star Schema Design
- MUST implement proper star schema with fact and dimension tables
- MUST use surrogate keys for dimension tables (sk_table_name pattern)
- MUST implement slowly changing dimensions (SCD) for historical tracking
- MUST use appropriate data types for optimal storage and performance
- MUST implement proper indexing strategies for large fact tables

## Query Performance
- MUST use appropriate partitioning strategies (date, region, product category)
- MUST implement columnar storage (Parquet) for analytical queries
- MUST use predicate pushdown for efficient filtering
- MUST avoid SELECT * in favor of explicit column selection
- MUST implement proper join strategies (broadcast, shuffle, sort-merge)

## Analytics Query Standards
- MUST use CTEs (Common Table Expressions) for complex multi-step queries
- MUST implement window functions for analytical calculations
- MUST use appropriate aggregation functions for business metrics
- MUST implement proper date/time handling for temporal analysis
- MUST use parameterized queries for dynamic reporting

## Data Quality in SQL
- MUST implement data validation checks in SQL transformations
- MUST handle null values appropriately in aggregations
- MUST implement referential integrity checks between tables
- MUST validate data ranges and business rule compliance
- MUST implement data lineage tracking in views and stored procedures

## View and Stored Procedure Standards
- MUST document all views with business purpose and usage
- MUST implement parameter validation in stored procedures
- MUST use consistent naming conventions (snake_case with _v or _sp suffix)
- MUST implement proper error handling and logging
- MUST optimize views for query performance

## Business Intelligence Support
- MUST implement standard metrics and KPIs consistently
- MUST support drill-down and roll-up operations
- MUST implement time-series analysis capabilities
- MUST support cohort and funnel analysis
- MUST provide data for dashboard and reporting tools

## Testing and Validation
- MUST include unit tests for complex SQL transformations
- MUST validate query results against expected business rules
- MUST implement performance testing for analytical queries
- MUST test data quality checks with known datasets
- MUST validate data consistency across related tables